<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Jan manufacturing output up 0.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Jan manufacturing output up 0.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch seasonally adjusted manufacturing production fell 3.4 percent in January compared with December, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>But January manufacturing production was 0.5 percent higher than in the same month of 1996, the CBS added.  </p>
<p>    DUTCH MANUFACTURING PRODUCTION    Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p>seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)			105.2     108.9     104.7</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	     -3.4	-0.4	-4.1</p>
<p>non-seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)			 99.9     110.2	99.4</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change		  0.5	-0.5	 1.1</p>
<p>NOTE - CBS calculates month-on-month changes on basis of seasonally adjusted index and year-on-year changes on basis of non-seasonally adjusted index.  </p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
